  "definition": {
    "active": "a conflict id is active in a calendar year with at least 25 battle-related deaths; a year with fewer is quiet",
    "battle_deaths_threshold": 25,
    "main": "the agreement first has to bring the fighting below the threshold: the clock starts at the first calendar year after signing in which no conflict id the agreement lists is active, and runs to the next active year (counted from the year before the first quiet year, so holding at 5 years means 5 or more quiet years in a row); agreements that never got below the threshold by 2024 are reported apart",
    "strict": "the clock starts at the signing year and runs to the first later active year, so fighting that never stopped counts as resumed",
    "settled_late": "the first quiet year came 5 or more years after signing, which is hard to credit to the agreement",
    "censoring": "agreements with no later active year are still holding when the data stop (2024)",
    "unit": "one agreement; agreements in linked conflicts are not independent",
    "figure_years": 20,
    "intervals": "main intervals: 95 % percentile cluster bootstrap over linked conflict groups (2000 resamples, seed 2026); Greenwood log-log intervals are kept for reference and are too narrow"
  },
